WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.234
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.601
Jay Hernandez. Welcome to the show, buddy.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.634
-Thank you, thank you. -I appreciate you being here.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.300
I love that "Magnum P.I." is now on NBC.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.701
-Yeah. -It's a big deal.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.300
-It's a big deal. -It's a big deal for us.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.434
-It doesn't happen often. You know, it's a very rare thing.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.067
-It is, but the fans spoke.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.734
-The fans spoke, and NBC listened.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.834
-They were loud. They were loud. They said, "Don't cancel.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.234
We love 'Magnum P.I.'" -What are you talking about?

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:23.934
Cancel after season four? No, not gonna happen.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.100
-But they actually put a billboard up in Times Square.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.234
Look at this.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:29.467
"Save 'Magnum P.I.'" With a QR code.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:32.434
-Yeah. Yeah. Hey, that's love. That is love.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.200
There was a petition online.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.300
They raised -- I don't know how much that costs.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.501
How much do you think it costs?

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.734
-I have no idea. That's insane.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.367
-It's not cheap. I know that. -That's amazing

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:43.334
that they were vocal and loud, and you got heard!

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.100
"Magnum P.I." is saved.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.267
This Sunday! -This Sunday.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:52.133
-Two-episode premiere on NBC. It's got to feel good.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:55.267
I mean, would you get nervous going into the Magnum P.I.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.367
shoes at first when they're like,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.367
"Hey, we want you to be Magnum P.I."?

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.901
-You know, what's funny is the first time they came to me

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.801
with the project, I think I said no twice

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:07.868
because I was convinced that nobody would accept

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:11.100
anybody else besides Tom Selleck as Magnum P.I.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.167
-Of course.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.501
-So it was a number of conversations.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.100
Ultimately I agreed to it.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.067
But it was somewhat intimidating, yes.

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.734
-You're like, "I can't step into those shoes."

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.534
I mean, come on. With the Detriot hat and all that stuff.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.968
-And the fuzzy chest and, you know --

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.334
-Yes. -And the short shorts.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.300
-He's a stud, man! Come on! -He had short shorts, too.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.067
-I know, dude. -Not only short shorts.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.934
It was short jeans. You know? Cutoff jeans.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.067
-But he pull anything off.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.667
-He could pull that off. That's hard to do.

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.067
Not too many people can do that.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.634
-What finally just convinced you?

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.033
What put you over the edge?

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.267
-I mean, I was a huge fan of the show.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.901
And ultimately, like, the creatives involved,

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:46.701
they pitched a show that I was like, "I can't say no to this."

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.467
Even, you know -- I don't know what's going to happen.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:49.767
I don't know if the show --

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.400
Because at the end of the day, it's a pilot.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.334
So you know it's a pilot.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:54.501
-Pilot is a trial show. -Right.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:55.901
-So you don't know if it's going to go.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.467
-You don't know if the show is going to go on

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:59.667
for one, two, three, four, five, ten seasons.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.000
You have no idea.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.634
-But it's also -- You're working in Hawaii.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:05.701
-Yeah, yeah. -I would take any job.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.534
You're playing the worst guy. Go, "I don't care.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.801
You said Hawaii. I'm there. I'll do whatever it is."

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.734
-I mean, it's funny coming here. You know, I was unprepared.

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.100
I was actually -- I thought I was going to need

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.634
a trench coat and a scarf.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.167
-You brought the great weather.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.534
-Yeah, I brought the warm weather.

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.734
-Yeah! Thank you! That's you! -You're welcome.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.534
-That's Jay Hernandez.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:27.400
-It's called the aloha vibes. You know what I mean? Yeah.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.300
-What is it like to live in Hawaii?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.734
Because now, you probably went, like you said for --

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.834
You go, "I'll shoot the show. It will be probably a couple weeks,

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.300
and then I'll come back home." -Yeah.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.701
-But now you live in --

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.667
-Now I'm pretty much there eight months out of the year.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.367
-And what's it like? What's the vibe?

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.834
-It's great. I mean, obviously, the weather is beautiful.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:46.734
But, you know, there is, like, aloha spirit

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.467
that is everywhere you go.

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.334
I mean, it's sunny. It's warm.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.133
Tourists get there, and they just want to have a good time.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.734
-Very positive. -Yeah. It's a positive vibe.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:59.033
It really sort of, like, seeps into you.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:00.400
-Everyone seems very chill there.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.000
-Very chill, very chill.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.033
I mean, maybe too chill because sometimes

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.267
you jump on the freeway and you see

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.801
that there's speed minimums,

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:09.968
which I've never seen anywhere else.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.267
-Wait. So not a speed limit.

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.067
-No, no, not a speed limit. A speed minimum.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.467
-So you have to go at least -- -Otherwise people would be

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.601
going 20 miles per hour on the freeway.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.667
-So they make you go a certain mile an hour?

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:22.100
-Yeah, the minimum I think was like 40 miles per hour.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.801
-That's so funny, man. -Because, otherwise, yeah.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:28.400
It's just -- It's a very mellow vibe out there. Yeah.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.734
-Well, what can we say for anyone?

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.267
We're setting up "Magnum P.I."

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.601
What's the adventures that Magnum gets into?

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:37.200
-Well, you know, there's a ton of action.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.834
There's always a bad guy.

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.734
There's always some crazy things going down --

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:43.934
cars, explosions, gun fights, all that kind of stuff.

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:45.901
But in this season that is unique

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.868
is Magnum and my partner, Higgins,

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.934
who is, you know, sort of my sidekick...

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.567
-What's that like? -It's great.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.334
But now we're --

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.801
-Have a sidekick named Higgins.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.467
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. -Sounds awful, yeah.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.968
-No, it's great. It's great. But we're together.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.534
We're dating essentially. -Yeah.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:04.968
-It's been wonderful, and it's something

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:07.534
that we've been teasing for three seasons now.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:10.133
So, season five is kind of the payoff for all that.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.367
-I'm happy that you're back at NBC, by the way.

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.200
-Yes, we just talked about it.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:18.300
It's a full-circle scenario because I started on NBC, like,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.234
20 years ago on a show called "Hang Time."

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:22.033
-"Hang Time" was one of my all-time --

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:25.133
-Does anyone remember this show? -Yes! It's one of my favorite!

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:27.334
With Anthony Anderson. -Yes, Anthony Anderson.

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:29.667
And when we were talking backstage...

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.267
he knew the theme song.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.667
-♪ Hang time, hanging together ♪

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.534
♪ Hang time ♪ [ Singing gibberish ]

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:37.734
♪ Hang time ♪

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.667
Dude, I watched you every Saturday morning.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:40.901
-So good.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.300
-I'm so happy you're back at NBC.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.400
-I love it.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.734
-Fans, let's bring back "Hang Time."

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.367
That's why we're here. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:49.000
Let's start with "Magnum P.I." This Sunday, "Magnum P.I."

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.434
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:51.968
Here's Jay Hernandez in the new season

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:54.067
of "Magnum P.I." Take a look.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:57.200
-You mind helping me put on sunscreen?

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.767
-Um...

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:00.968
-Just on the parts I can't reach.

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:02.601
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.801
Don't you have somebody do that for you?

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.701
-Well, I certainly don't have a boyfriend,

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.267
if that's what you're getting at.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.067
-No, no, no. That's not what I'm saying.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:13.634
It's just that technically I'm on safety patrol right now,

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.501
so I really --

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:18.901
-Oh, well, sunburn definitely falls under safety.

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:22.868
-Well, you're not wrong.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:25.367
Yeah, it does.

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:28.067
Uh, okay.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:32.234
So just, um...

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:35.801
And, uh, rub it in. Yeah?

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:40.667
-Hey, Robbie. -Hey. Hey!

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:42.667
-"Oh, hey! Hi!"

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.133
-"Oh!" -"Whoa!"

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.767
-Jay Hernandez.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.801
"Magnum P.I." premieres with two episodes

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:49.701
this Sunday at 9:00 p.m. on NBC.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:52.868
Streams the next day on Peacock. More "Tonight Show"

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.133
after the break. Stick around, everybody.

